  t inverts T, <a_0,e_delta>=T[2].                      (9)

Here D is split if -delta is a square.  Consequently

  h=|D^1|=q-epsilon_delta,   |Q_delta|=2h^2,
  Inv(Q_delta)=(T[2]-{1}) disjoint-union Tt,
  |Inv(Q_delta)|=3+h^2.                                 (10)

